1
00:00:10,146 --> 00:00:12,606
PLANT PRODUCTION RESEARCH FACILITY

2
00:00:12,690 --> 00:00:16,026
[Haru humming softly]

3
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:29,790
[Mika] I wonder where Haru went.

4
00:00:29,874 --> 00:00:32,084
[Lisa] We need to hurry
or there won't be any seats left.

5
00:00:32,168 --> 00:00:33,669
- [Mika] Yeah, that's right!
- [Kimi] She in there?

6
00:00:33,753 --> 00:00:34,628
[Mika] Err...

7
00:00:34,712 --> 00:00:36,297
- [Lisa] Hey, Haru!
- [Haru gasps]

8
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:38,382
[Lisa] So this is where
you've been hiding.

9
00:00:38,466 --> 00:00:40,509
Second period's over, you know.

10
00:00:40,593 --> 00:00:42,553
[Haru sighs] I can't leave a gap
in the records.

11
00:00:42,636 --> 00:00:44,013
It'll affect my grades.

12
00:00:44,096 --> 00:00:45,431
Where's Professor Dorin?

13
00:00:45,514 --> 00:00:47,308
Oh, well she already took off.

14
00:00:47,391 --> 00:00:49,351
Hey, we don't have all day.
Let's hurry up.

15
00:00:49,435 --> 00:00:51,520
We gotta be quick
if we want a seat for lunch.

16
00:00:51,604 --> 00:00:53,814
- [Kimi] Mm-hm.
- Oh, I'm sorry. Just go on ahead.

17
00:00:54,607 --> 00:00:57,735
Aw... How about we order for you?
Does that sound okay?

18
00:00:57,818 --> 00:00:58,778
[Haru] Yeah, that's great.

19
00:00:58,861 --> 00:01:00,905
[Lisa] They should totally give us
more time for lunch.

20
00:01:00,988 --> 00:01:01,822
[Kimi] Seriously!

21
00:01:01,906 --> 00:01:04,533
[Lisa] If there are any seats left,
I'll be shocked.

22
00:01:06,368 --> 00:01:07,661
[humming]

23
00:01:08,871 --> 00:01:10,206
[chuckles softly]

24
00:01:14,168 --> 00:01:17,838
- [loud thud]
- What? Huh? What was that?

25
00:01:23,511 --> 00:01:24,470
Um...

26
00:01:27,264 --> 00:01:28,098
Hm?

27
00:01:28,641 --> 00:01:30,810
[intriguing music playing]

28
00:01:32,770 --> 00:01:33,938
[gasps]

29
00:01:38,692 --> 00:01:39,527
[gasps]

30
00:01:40,027 --> 00:01:42,947
Huh? What in the world?

31
00:01:45,699 --> 00:01:47,034
Professor Dorin!

32
00:01:47,993 --> 00:01:50,996
Professor? Professor, can you hear me?

33
00:01:52,790 --> 00:01:56,836
A-Anyone? Uh, I need help! Anyone!

34
00:01:56,919 --> 00:01:58,129
[feather rustles]

35
00:02:03,425 --> 00:02:04,260
[sighs]

36
00:02:04,343 --> 00:02:05,177
[male student] What's wrong?

37
00:02:05,803 --> 00:02:07,763
{\an8}We need an ambulance right now!

38
00:02:07,847 --> 00:02:09,056
[male student] Oh no, Professor Dorin!

39
00:02:09,140 --> 00:02:12,393
I'll go get help.
I need a doctor! Someone call a doctor!

40
00:02:12,476 --> 00:02:14,061
[tense music playing]

41
00:02:14,145 --> 00:02:16,939
[female student 1] What happened?
Can they still be alive?

42
00:02:17,022 --> 00:02:18,232
[female student 2]
Did she fall from the roof?

43
00:02:18,315 --> 00:02:19,650
[female student 3] Stay back!
Don't touch her!

44
00:02:21,735 --> 00:02:23,904
[opening theme music playing]

45
00:03:51,033 --> 00:03:55,955
A THREEFOLD DILEMMA

46
00:03:56,038 --> 00:03:57,831
[waves crashing]

47
00:04:04,421 --> 00:04:08,092
[Melon] Do you want to know
what my favorite thing in the world is?

48
00:04:08,175 --> 00:04:09,051
[Legoshi choking]

49
00:04:09,134 --> 00:04:12,179
{\an8}The face of someone afraid of death.

50
00:04:12,763 --> 00:04:17,726
{\an8}No matter what species they are,
everybody makes the same one without fail.

51
00:04:17,810 --> 00:04:22,481
{\an8}Not a lie to be found,
a face that is genuinely honest.

52
00:04:22,564 --> 00:04:23,649
{\an8}[straining]

53
00:04:23,732 --> 00:04:25,609
{\an8}[Melon laughs maniacally]

54
00:04:25,693 --> 00:04:31,573
{\an8}- Yes, that's the one! That face there...
- [choking]

55
00:04:32,449 --> 00:04:33,742
[Melon] Uh-oh.

56
00:04:42,418 --> 00:04:43,419
[muffled grunting]

57
00:04:44,003 --> 00:04:48,048
[muffled groaning]

58
00:05:01,228 --> 00:05:03,522
[muffled mumbling]

59
00:05:04,481 --> 00:05:06,817
[fish babbling indistinctly]

60
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,111
[Legoshi] <i>I have no idea
what they're saying.</i>

61
00:05:09,194 --> 00:05:11,655
<i>I should have studied Oceanic languages.</i>

62
00:05:11,739 --> 00:05:13,115
[fish shrieking in fear]

63
00:05:17,244 --> 00:05:19,288
[suspenseful music playing]

64
00:05:20,956 --> 00:05:22,249
[muffled groaning]

65
00:05:26,003 --> 00:05:27,379
[muffled grunting]

66
00:05:39,892 --> 00:05:43,228
<i>Oh, I can't hold my breath anymore.</i>

67
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:52,488
Agaga papubu daba goma beeda!

68
00:05:54,281 --> 00:05:58,243
Agaga papubu daba goma beeda!

69
00:06:05,834 --> 00:06:06,960
[muffled giggling]

70
00:06:09,254 --> 00:06:10,339
[muffled shrieking]

71
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,475
[tranquil melody playing]

72
00:06:29,942 --> 00:06:31,235
[groans softly]

73
00:06:41,995 --> 00:06:44,414
[muffled] Thank you for the help!

74
00:06:45,082 --> 00:06:47,626
<i>Uh... I feel bad.</i>

75
00:06:47,709 --> 00:06:50,003
<i>I should at least know
how to say thank you.</i>

76
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:53,340
[gurgling]

77
00:06:55,092 --> 00:06:56,510
[gasps]

78
00:07:03,934 --> 00:07:05,936
[Legoshi knocking on door] Mr. Sagwan?

79
00:07:07,312 --> 00:07:09,481
- [clothes whoosh, zipper swishes]
- Hello?

80
00:07:09,565 --> 00:07:11,483
- [footsteps approaching]
- Are you home?

81
00:07:14,278 --> 00:07:16,530
Oh, it's just you, Legoshi.

82
00:07:16,613 --> 00:07:18,615
Looks like I got dressed for nothing.

83
00:07:18,699 --> 00:07:22,077
Uh, sorry for stopping by so unannounced.

84
00:07:22,161 --> 00:07:25,289
[Sagwan sniffing]
Well, you smell just like home.

85
00:07:25,998 --> 00:07:28,542
Did you... take a dip in the ocean?

86
00:07:28,625 --> 00:07:33,422
Uh, actually... I did, and I almost drowned.

87
00:07:33,505 --> 00:07:34,590
What?

88
00:07:37,384 --> 00:07:40,262
[slow reggae music playing]

89
00:07:40,345 --> 00:07:43,140
So the shark,
he was about to have me for dinner.

90
00:07:43,223 --> 00:07:46,059
Uh. And then I remembered
the magic words you taught me.

91
00:07:46,643 --> 00:07:49,354
What magic words were those?

92
00:07:49,438 --> 00:07:52,149
Agaga papubu daba goma beeda!

93
00:07:53,192 --> 00:07:54,401
Ah!

94
00:07:54,902 --> 00:07:57,779
I really think that saved me.

95
00:07:58,739 --> 00:08:00,574
What does it mean anyway?

96
00:08:00,657 --> 00:08:02,534
Nothing fancy.

97
00:08:02,618 --> 00:08:04,995
All it means
is that you have a special friend

98
00:08:05,078 --> 00:08:09,082
who just happens to be
a spotted seal! [chuckles]

99
00:08:11,793 --> 00:08:13,045
Uh...

100
00:08:14,713 --> 00:08:15,839
All right.

101
00:08:16,423 --> 00:08:20,511
So I guess spotted seals have some kind
of high status in the ocean then.

102
00:08:20,594 --> 00:08:23,138
- Here you go, my kelp tea.
- Oh, that's hot. Hmm...

103
00:08:23,222 --> 00:08:25,933
Friendships can save lives, you know.

104
00:08:26,517 --> 00:08:29,186
We have the kind of friendship
with nothing to hide.

105
00:08:29,770 --> 00:08:31,522
That's a special thing!

106
00:08:31,605 --> 00:08:35,609
- Ah. Smells like the sea, doesn't it?
- Hmm?

107
00:08:35,692 --> 00:08:37,319
Hold on, look at that.

108
00:08:37,402 --> 00:08:39,696
- [Legoshi] Huh?
- Your ear is a mess!

109
00:08:40,489 --> 00:08:41,406
[Legoshi] Uh...

110
00:08:48,247 --> 00:08:49,790
<i>Melon shot me.</i>

111
00:08:49,873 --> 00:08:52,709
<i>And the worst part?
He was thrilled about it.</i>

112
00:08:53,418 --> 00:08:54,419
[gunshot]

113
00:08:55,045 --> 00:08:56,088
Wow.

114
00:08:56,171 --> 00:09:01,510
You really do live in a fantasy world,
don't you, Wolfie Boy? [chuckles]

115
00:09:02,344 --> 00:09:06,223
[Legoshi] <i>What's wrong with that?
It's my life, not his.</i>

116
00:09:06,306 --> 00:09:09,059
{\an8}I'm doing it because it's so much fun.

117
00:09:09,142 --> 00:09:11,979
{\an8}How could it not be
when someone so full of hope

118
00:09:12,062 --> 00:09:13,814
{\an8}falls into the grip of despair?

119
00:09:13,897 --> 00:09:15,732
- [Legoshi] <i>Damn him.</i>
- [Melon laughing maniacally]

120
00:09:15,816 --> 00:09:16,942
[Legoshi] <i>He was laughing.</i>

121
00:09:17,025 --> 00:09:18,235
[crystal shatters]

122
00:09:18,318 --> 00:09:21,238
<i>It's not just wrong. It's evil.</i>

123
00:09:21,822 --> 00:09:23,574
<i>Evil does exist.</i>

124
00:09:26,118 --> 00:09:27,828
CITY HALL

125
00:09:27,911 --> 00:09:29,538
FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR

126
00:09:29,621 --> 00:09:33,792
{\an8}We thank Louis,
the brave heir to the Horns Conglomerate,

127
00:09:33,875 --> 00:09:36,878
for his important contribution to society.

128
00:09:37,462 --> 00:09:41,592
It's his brave efforts that have revealed
the real dangers of Kines.

129
00:09:42,301 --> 00:09:45,387
It's my honor
to present this award to him.

130
00:09:45,470 --> 00:09:47,723
This is our highest commendation.

131
00:09:47,806 --> 00:09:49,516
[camera shutters clicking]

132
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:53,604
I have to say, I've had the pleasure
of knowing Louis here

133
00:09:53,687 --> 00:09:56,565
since he was a young student at Cherryton.

134
00:09:56,648 --> 00:10:00,360
Even back then I could tell
that he possessed a special spark,

135
00:10:01,194 --> 00:10:04,531
- just like his distinguished father.
- [Louis scoffs]

136
00:10:07,534 --> 00:10:10,162
Louis showed his character
by acting alone on this.

137
00:10:10,787 --> 00:10:15,334
He showed initiative,
and didn't run away from responsibility.

138
00:10:15,417 --> 00:10:19,963
This is why I consider him worthy
of becoming the next Beastar!

139
00:10:20,047 --> 00:10:21,048
[Louis] Uh--

140
00:10:21,923 --> 00:10:26,637
He's a strong Beastar candidate,
who I'm honored to give my support.

141
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:27,846
[grunts softly]

142
00:10:29,264 --> 00:10:31,933
[Mayor] This is the black market
live bait records.

143
00:10:32,017 --> 00:10:33,810
Your name is still in here.

144
00:10:34,478 --> 00:10:38,106
All you have to do
is keep quiet about this... business here,

145
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:40,692
and just make sure
the festival runs smoothly.

146
00:10:41,693 --> 00:10:44,738
I'll make this disappear.
I'll erase this for you.

147
00:10:46,323 --> 00:10:48,825
<i>Your dark past vanishes.</i>

148
00:10:52,746 --> 00:10:54,247
[Louis sighs]

149
00:10:55,123 --> 00:10:56,541
[Mayor] Mmm?

150
00:10:56,625 --> 00:10:59,670
- [camera shutters clicking]
- [slow guitar music playing]

151
00:11:09,471 --> 00:11:12,265
Excuse me! You're Louis, aren't you?

152
00:11:12,349 --> 00:11:16,603
- Oh, sorry, but I'm in a bit of a hurry.
- It's just, well, I had to thank you.

153
00:11:18,271 --> 00:11:20,065
{\an8}My friend was attacked.

154
00:11:20,148 --> 00:11:22,859
{\an8}The carnivore who did it
was drinking Kines.

155
00:11:23,402 --> 00:11:24,903
{\an8}I tried to help, and then...

156
00:11:25,487 --> 00:11:26,571
[gasps softly]

157
00:11:26,655 --> 00:11:29,074
It doesn't hurt all the time,
just sometimes.

158
00:11:29,699 --> 00:11:30,617
I'm sorry.

159
00:11:31,451 --> 00:11:35,664
There were a lot of rumors about Kines,
but no one did anything about it.

160
00:11:36,373 --> 00:11:38,166
{\an8}Until you came along.

161
00:11:39,292 --> 00:11:41,920
Anyway, thank you for caring.

162
00:11:48,468 --> 00:11:49,469
Hmm.

163
00:11:54,057 --> 00:11:55,267
YASUMARU FAMILY PHARMACY

164
00:11:55,350 --> 00:11:56,977
[male pharmacist] Thanks, take care!

165
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,188
[sniffles]

166
00:12:01,189 --> 00:12:02,399
[moans softly]

167
00:12:06,236 --> 00:12:08,238
[Seven] They invited me to a fancy dinner,

168
00:12:08,321 --> 00:12:10,949
but it turns out they just wanted me
to be the hostess!

169
00:12:11,032 --> 00:12:12,659
Like, seriously?

170
00:12:12,742 --> 00:12:14,870
Am I supposed to be
some fluffy piece of wool

171
00:12:14,953 --> 00:12:17,289
for an old carnivore
to stick his teeth into?

172
00:12:17,372 --> 00:12:18,457
I didn't sign up for that,

173
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,125
- thank you very much.
- [Legoshi sneezes]

174
00:12:20,208 --> 00:12:21,168
Huh?

175
00:12:21,251 --> 00:12:23,420
Hey, so you catch colds too, huh?

176
00:12:23,503 --> 00:12:24,796
[Legoshi sniffles]

177
00:12:26,131 --> 00:12:28,300
I'm not feeling too good.

178
00:12:28,383 --> 00:12:30,802
[Seven] What do wolves do
when they catch a cold?

179
00:12:30,886 --> 00:12:33,555
Oh, usually soup or something.

180
00:12:33,638 --> 00:12:36,850
But I remember when I was a kid,
they'd put cabbage on my head.

181
00:12:36,933 --> 00:12:38,643
[Seven chuckles] Does that really work?

182
00:12:38,727 --> 00:12:40,562
My grandpa tells me it does.

183
00:12:40,645 --> 00:12:41,646
Uh--

184
00:12:44,399 --> 00:12:45,442
Legoshi.

185
00:12:45,525 --> 00:12:47,360
[Legoshi] Eh-- um, Louis, sir...

186
00:12:47,444 --> 00:12:50,572
Oh, I... I see you're busy. Another time.

187
00:12:50,655 --> 00:12:53,575
Oh, no, no,
this is not what you're thinking.

188
00:12:53,658 --> 00:12:54,618
Just hang on!

189
00:12:54,701 --> 00:12:56,286
Hey, what's going on?
Is he your boyfriend?

190
00:12:56,369 --> 00:12:57,829
Oh, it's not that either!

191
00:12:57,913 --> 00:12:59,664
Whatever. Take this.

192
00:13:00,415 --> 00:13:02,250
Don't forget to take your medicine.

193
00:13:03,084 --> 00:13:06,213
[chuckles nervously] Her...
She's just my neighbor.

194
00:13:06,296 --> 00:13:08,048
Of course, whatever you say.

195
00:13:08,131 --> 00:13:10,342
But it's not like that... [sneezes]

196
00:13:12,844 --> 00:13:14,763
Seriously, Haru's the only girl for me.

197
00:13:14,846 --> 00:13:16,806
It's all right, none of my business.

198
00:13:17,432 --> 00:13:18,600
[Legoshi sniffles]

199
00:13:19,184 --> 00:13:20,477
I fell into the ocean.

200
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:21,811
Huh? The ocean?

201
00:13:21,895 --> 00:13:24,856
So you'll have to forgive me.
I know I look a little rough.

202
00:13:24,940 --> 00:13:28,360
Well, I brought something
that might make you feel better.

203
00:13:32,197 --> 00:13:34,241
Here. Take your medicine.

204
00:13:34,324 --> 00:13:36,326
Ah, yeah, good idea.

205
00:13:37,577 --> 00:13:41,164
Your job doesn't really seem to care
about your privacy.

206
00:13:41,748 --> 00:13:44,709
They told me where you lived
and they drew me a map.

207
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:50,715
So you went to the Udon restaurant
just to meet with me?

208
00:13:52,259 --> 00:13:53,843
What's going on?

209
00:13:53,927 --> 00:13:57,639
Well, first things first,
I have a few gifts for you here.

210
00:13:57,722 --> 00:13:59,724
Which of these three do you want to eat?

211
00:14:00,642 --> 00:14:01,476
Jelly?

212
00:14:01,977 --> 00:14:03,311
Sponge cake?

213
00:14:03,395 --> 00:14:04,229
Or me?

214
00:14:05,730 --> 00:14:07,649
[coughing] Back up a sec!

215
00:14:08,233 --> 00:14:11,486
Just a little carnivore humor I thought of
on my way over here.

216
00:14:11,570 --> 00:14:12,654
It's not funny.

217
00:14:13,238 --> 00:14:14,865
{\an8}So did something happen or what?

218
00:14:15,490 --> 00:14:17,492
I came here to check in on you.

219
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:18,994
Huh?

220
00:14:19,494 --> 00:14:21,788
[Louis sighs] It seems
I had a premonition.

221
00:14:21,872 --> 00:14:25,292
Then I learned you fell into the ocean,
and look at your ear.

222
00:14:25,375 --> 00:14:27,168
What have you gotten yourself into?

223
00:14:27,252 --> 00:14:29,421
You came because
you were worried about me?

224
00:14:29,504 --> 00:14:31,548
And? Is there a problem with that?

225
00:14:31,631 --> 00:14:33,133
Hmm, not really.

226
00:14:33,216 --> 00:14:35,927
Listen, I had a feeling
something had happened to you.

227
00:14:37,095 --> 00:14:39,431
My right leg was having phantom pains.

228
00:14:39,514 --> 00:14:40,348
[Legoshi] What?

229
00:14:41,057 --> 00:14:42,309
[Louis] It's happened twice before.

230
00:14:43,059 --> 00:14:44,019
Oh.

231
00:14:44,102 --> 00:14:46,271
Did something else happen, Legoshi?

232
00:14:46,354 --> 00:14:49,524
Uh, well, I could ask
the same question to you.

233
00:14:49,608 --> 00:14:51,151
- Huh?
- What about all those scratches?

234
00:14:51,234 --> 00:14:52,360
What happened to your face?

235
00:14:53,069 --> 00:14:55,363
You know what else?
I saw you on television.

236
00:14:55,447 --> 00:14:59,034
You got an award at the police station.
Man, I thought that was so awesome.

237
00:14:59,117 --> 00:15:00,827
You don't even have a television.

238
00:15:00,911 --> 00:15:02,787
- I do at work.
- [Louis scoffs]

239
00:15:04,706 --> 00:15:08,418
It wasn't anything special.
It actually made me angry.

240
00:15:09,002 --> 00:15:10,921
It's not like everything's
wrapped up in a bow.

241
00:15:11,755 --> 00:15:13,465
[Legoshi] You talking about Kines?

242
00:15:13,548 --> 00:15:17,052
[Louis sighs] Someone was pushing it
into the public's hands,

243
00:15:17,135 --> 00:15:19,429
targeting children
who don't know any better.

244
00:15:19,971 --> 00:15:21,306
I can't let that go.

245
00:15:21,848 --> 00:15:24,559
[Legoshi] I bet a lot of herbivores
were saved because of you.

246
00:15:24,643 --> 00:15:25,685
You should be proud.

247
00:15:25,769 --> 00:15:27,145
That's not the point.

248
00:15:27,228 --> 00:15:29,397
I wanted to help the carnivores too,
you know.

249
00:15:30,065 --> 00:15:32,609
Someone had to keep that stuff away
from you idiots.

250
00:15:33,193 --> 00:15:35,654
Carnivores need saving from themselves.

251
00:15:37,614 --> 00:15:38,531
Here.

252
00:15:38,615 --> 00:15:39,950
Oh, thank you, sir.

253
00:15:42,577 --> 00:15:45,580
Well. Tell me what happened to you.

254
00:15:47,832 --> 00:15:53,004
Well, uh... Hmm. Where do I start?

255
00:15:53,088 --> 00:15:55,882
- I was chasing a bad guy.
- Really?

256
00:15:55,966 --> 00:15:58,551
And the thing is, the Beastar asked me to.

257
00:15:58,635 --> 00:15:59,469
What?

258
00:15:59,552 --> 00:16:01,388
But then I kinda wanted to talk to him,

259
00:16:01,471 --> 00:16:03,682
- so I tried to go find where he was.
- Go on.

260
00:16:04,307 --> 00:16:05,392
Uh...

261
00:16:05,976 --> 00:16:07,644
- I got shot.
- [Louis exclaims]

262
00:16:07,727 --> 00:16:09,646
[grunts] When was this?

263
00:16:09,729 --> 00:16:12,440
It was during last month's
crescent moon, I think.

264
00:16:13,024 --> 00:16:14,693
- I actually died once.
- Huh?

265
00:16:14,776 --> 00:16:17,070
And while I was dead,
my mother came to me.

266
00:16:17,153 --> 00:16:18,446
She said something like,

267
00:16:18,530 --> 00:16:20,740
"It's important to say
what you want to say."

268
00:16:20,824 --> 00:16:21,908
Huh?

269
00:16:21,992 --> 00:16:23,326
I thought, "Yeah, she's right."

270
00:16:23,410 --> 00:16:26,788
Then I came back to life
during the full moon.

271
00:16:26,871 --> 00:16:31,751
Then I went to a meeting with him,
and then I got this-- Got shot again.

272
00:16:31,835 --> 00:16:32,794
[Louis] What?

273
00:16:32,877 --> 00:16:34,629
That's when I went in the ocean.

274
00:16:34,713 --> 00:16:36,339
[sniffles, sneezes]

275
00:16:37,882 --> 00:16:38,883
Bless me.

276
00:16:41,094 --> 00:16:43,138
Then what? Where's the guy?

277
00:16:43,221 --> 00:16:45,515
Uh, still out there, I guess.

278
00:16:45,598 --> 00:16:47,600
Even after you went through all that.

279
00:16:47,684 --> 00:16:49,561
Oh, the Shishi-Gumi were there as well.

280
00:16:50,562 --> 00:16:51,396
Hmm.

281
00:16:53,064 --> 00:16:55,817
Wait, this guy... Was he a mix?

282
00:16:55,900 --> 00:16:59,487
Mmm, yeah. He's gazelle and leopard.

283
00:16:59,571 --> 00:17:00,572
Melon!

284
00:17:01,406 --> 00:17:03,575
Huh? So you know who this guy is?

285
00:17:04,325 --> 00:17:06,119
Uh, hang on. Wait.

286
00:17:06,202 --> 00:17:08,663
Didn't you say
you cut all ties with the Shishi-Gumi,

287
00:17:08,747 --> 00:17:09,956
that you were done with them?

288
00:17:10,040 --> 00:17:12,208
I ran into them
when I was investigating Kines.

289
00:17:12,292 --> 00:17:16,129
Uh, so-- so are you saying
that you've met Melon too?

290
00:17:16,838 --> 00:17:20,050
{\an8}Not really, I just saw Melon
from a hiding spot.

291
00:17:20,133 --> 00:17:22,594
{\an8}But the one spreading Kines
into the general public?

292
00:17:22,677 --> 00:17:24,012
{\an8}I know it was him.

293
00:17:24,637 --> 00:17:26,139
{\an8}Pretty ironic, huh?

294
00:17:26,222 --> 00:17:29,184
{\an8}That's how the Shishi-Gumi
were rebuilding their business.

295
00:17:29,976 --> 00:17:31,186
{\an8}But never mind that.

296
00:17:31,269 --> 00:17:32,979
{\an8}Why did you go to a meeting with Melon?

297
00:17:33,063 --> 00:17:35,523
Oh, well, uh...

298
00:17:35,607 --> 00:17:37,609
You had to know that he was dangerous.

299
00:17:38,693 --> 00:17:39,611
Uh...

300
00:17:40,779 --> 00:17:43,073
I-I just wanted to know...

301
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:47,786
what he feels.
Why he thinks the way he does.

302
00:17:49,037 --> 00:17:52,207
I thought maybe if we talked,
I could understand him better.

303
00:17:53,666 --> 00:17:55,460
{\an8}Boy, was I wrong.

304
00:17:55,543 --> 00:17:57,253
{\an8}There's no getting through to him.

305
00:17:57,337 --> 00:17:58,755
Huh?

306
00:18:00,048 --> 00:18:00,924
[Louis] Hmm.

307
00:18:01,841 --> 00:18:04,844
Well, looks like you have quite a fever.

308
00:18:06,179 --> 00:18:08,848
We'll talk another time.
Sorry for just dropping by.

309
00:18:08,932 --> 00:18:10,725
- No problem.
- All right.

310
00:18:10,809 --> 00:18:12,102
Uh... Bye.

311
00:18:15,897 --> 00:18:18,525
[Louis sighs] When you feel better,
we'll talk again.

312
00:18:23,029 --> 00:18:27,826
Melon, uh... He just enjoys it, I guess.

313
00:18:28,576 --> 00:18:31,871
Tearing everyone apart is fun for him.

314
00:18:33,373 --> 00:18:34,582
It's not about reason.

315
00:18:35,708 --> 00:18:38,169
I saw it in his eyes in that moment.

316
00:18:39,754 --> 00:18:44,175
Right when he let me drop,
his eyes were so alive,

317
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:49,514
like there were fires
blazing from inside. [shudders]

318
00:18:52,016 --> 00:18:55,186
It's okay. Just get some rest for now.

319
00:18:57,188 --> 00:19:00,650
I, uh... I'm scared.

320
00:19:02,861 --> 00:19:06,072
[Louis] <i>My friend, what are you afraid of?</i>

321
00:19:11,995 --> 00:19:13,788
[Mika] It just won't end, huh?

322
00:19:13,872 --> 00:19:16,332
- [Kimi] I wouldn't take that bet.
- [Lisa] Right, right. You're so right.

323
00:19:16,416 --> 00:19:18,877
- [Mika] So, Haru, are you all right?
- [Haru] Huh?

324
00:19:19,544 --> 00:19:22,046
Didn't you see what happened
to Professor Dorin?

325
00:19:22,130 --> 00:19:24,090
[Kimi] Hey, maybe now's not the time.

326
00:19:24,174 --> 00:19:26,092
I'm just checking in
with my friend is all.

327
00:19:26,176 --> 00:19:27,051
[Haru] I didn't see anything.

328
00:19:27,135 --> 00:19:29,512
I heard a loud noise
and then she was just lying there.

329
00:19:29,596 --> 00:19:30,555
[Mika] Mmm.

330
00:19:30,638 --> 00:19:34,350
I feel bad. We ran off to lunch
and just left you all alone.

331
00:19:34,434 --> 00:19:36,227
I'm really sorry, Haru.

332
00:19:36,311 --> 00:19:39,814
Oh, well, it's okay.
It's just a bit of a shock.

333
00:19:39,898 --> 00:19:40,899
I don't know.

334
00:19:40,982 --> 00:19:43,693
Could the railing on the roof
have just given out like that?

335
00:19:43,776 --> 00:19:45,904
Dunno, it's not like
the building is ancient.

336
00:19:45,987 --> 00:19:47,280
[Lisa] Well, you want to hear some tea?

337
00:19:47,363 --> 00:19:48,198
- [Kimi] Tell me.
- [Mika] What?

338
00:19:48,281 --> 00:19:50,116
This is just what I heard,

339
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:54,204
but apparently Professor Dorin
didn't have many fans on the board.

340
00:19:54,287 --> 00:19:57,123
- Sounds like they really didn't like her.
- Is that true?

341
00:19:57,207 --> 00:19:59,167
Well, from what I heard
about the professor,

342
00:19:59,250 --> 00:20:00,835
she was drunk with power.

343
00:20:00,919 --> 00:20:02,128
And because of that,

344
00:20:02,212 --> 00:20:05,173
she didn't win the election
to become board chairman.

345
00:20:05,256 --> 00:20:08,259
The university is saying
that it was some kind of accident,

346
00:20:08,343 --> 00:20:10,595
but there's a rumor that it was suicide.

347
00:20:10,678 --> 00:20:11,888
- [Mika] Really?
- [Lisa] I don't know.

348
00:20:11,971 --> 00:20:13,932
- Would she really kill herself?
- These are just rumors.

349
00:20:14,015 --> 00:20:15,808
It's not like there were
any eyewitnesses, right?

350
00:20:15,892 --> 00:20:17,602
Maybe someone saw but didn't come forward.

351
00:20:17,685 --> 00:20:18,519
[Mika] Oh, that's spooky.

352
00:20:18,603 --> 00:20:22,315
Sorry, guys.
I think I'm just gonna go home.

353
00:20:23,316 --> 00:20:24,859
- [Mika] Yeah.
- [Lisa] Hmm.

354
00:20:26,819 --> 00:20:28,404
What did we say?

355
00:20:29,155 --> 00:20:31,366
RESTRICTED AREA. KEEP OUT.

356
00:20:41,251 --> 00:20:42,543
[sighs]

357
00:20:44,504 --> 00:20:47,215
What? Oh, Professor Lumrong.

358
00:20:47,298 --> 00:20:52,053
Oh, you're that student who's always
so chatty during my classes. [chuckles]

359
00:20:52,720 --> 00:20:54,264
Yeah, probably me.

360
00:21:00,103 --> 00:21:03,022
Were you taking Professor Dorin's class?

361
00:21:03,564 --> 00:21:05,149
Oh, oh, no.

362
00:21:05,233 --> 00:21:07,151
I'm just here to pay respects, is all.

363
00:21:07,986 --> 00:21:11,739
I see. She shared a lot of wisdom with me.

364
00:21:12,282 --> 00:21:13,700
[Haru] It's such a shame.

365
00:21:14,284 --> 00:21:16,327
An unfortunate accident.

366
00:21:18,121 --> 00:21:22,041
Well, uh, it was an accident... right?

367
00:21:22,125 --> 00:21:23,918
- [intriguing music playing]
- Hmm?

368
00:21:24,002 --> 00:21:25,837
What are you implying?

369
00:21:26,421 --> 00:21:27,672
It's just...

370
00:21:29,048 --> 00:21:32,427
I just feel like someone else was there.

371
00:21:33,761 --> 00:21:37,265
Have you shared these thoughts?

372
00:21:37,348 --> 00:21:39,434
[Haru] Uh, forget I said
anything about it.

373
00:21:39,517 --> 00:21:42,270
I mean, I'm not trying
to make anyone a suspect here.

374
00:21:42,353 --> 00:21:44,272
Hmm, I see.

375
00:21:45,481 --> 00:21:48,901
If it's okay with you,
I'd like to hear what you think happened.

376
00:21:48,985 --> 00:21:50,069
[Haru] Yeah, but...

377
00:21:50,153 --> 00:21:53,698
Don't carry such a burden
on those little shoulders.

378
00:21:53,781 --> 00:21:57,702
If you don't mind,
let's have a chat in my office, hmm?

379
00:22:01,080 --> 00:22:03,374
[closing theme song playing]
